 "decisions": [
  {
   "what": "Requirements taken from hifi-receiver-2 docs/product.md and plan.md item 21; no open questions to the person",
   "why": "The person said 'Done = fab files complete' and the product doc fixes the board's contents; the FFC pinout is proposed to the core board's run (261028-145641) and matched if theirs differs",
   "phase": "P0",
   "ts": "2026-10-28T11:17:20"
  },
  {
   "what": "No research agents spawned; datasheets read inline (LCD HS20HS072RX, IRM-H638T, TCA9535, TS-1187A, RGB LED, EC11)",
   "why": "A passive UI board with two simple ICs; every wiring fact comes from a datasheet page cited in the README",
   "phase": "P1",
   "ts": "2026-10-28T11:17:21"
  },
  {
   "what": "Designing under coverage gap: led-indicator and load-switch blocks have no checklist; TCA9535 and IRM-H638T have no extraction JSON",
   "why": "Trivial blocks (a resistor-fed LED, a logic-level FET switching 60 mA); the IR receiver's RC filter is the datasheet's application circuit; research budget not worth spending",
   "phase": "P2",
   "ts": "2026-10-28T11:17:22"
  },
  {
   "what": "An I2C expander (TCA9535, 0x27) carries encoder, buttons, LED and LCD reset; only SPI(4)+BL PWM+INT+IR reach ESP32 GPIOs, ENC_A/B also brought out direct",
   "why": "The core's ESP32-WROVER-E has Ethernet RMII, two I2S and I2C on it and very few free GPIOs",
   "phase": "P2",
   "ts": "2026-10-28T11:17:22"
  },
  {
   "what": "FFC power pins mirror-symmetric (1/20 GND, 2/19 +3V3, 3/18 +5V)",
   "why": "FFC cable type A/B decides whether pin 1 lands on pin 1 or 20; a reversed cable then only swaps signals, never shorts a rail",
   "phase": "P2",
   "ts": "2026-10-28T11:17:22"
  },
  {
   "what": "LCD connector is double-sided contact (FPC-05FB-12PH20)",
   "why": "The LCD tail's contacts face the display side; with the panel lying on the board the tail enters face-up, and a dual-contact connector removes the orientation risk",
   "phase": "P2",
   "ts": "2026-10-28T11:17:22"
  },
  {
   "what": "Backlight from +5V through 2 x 75R 0603 in parallel (37.5R, 49-59 mA), low-side AO3400A, 100k gate pull-down",
   "why": "From 3V3 the 2.8-3.2 V LEDs leave no headroom; 33R 1206 is not a JLC basic part, two basic 75R 0603 share 55 mW each",
   "phase": "P2",
   "ts": "2026-10-28T11:17:23"
  },
  {
   "what": "RGB LED common anode on +5V, cathodes sunk by TCA9535 (5 V tolerant I/O); off = pin as input",
   "why": "Green/blue Vf ~3 V needs more than 3.3 V; high-Z off leaves no current path",
   "phase": "P2",
   "ts": "2026-10-28T11:17:23"
  },
  {
   "what": "All parts LCSC; Basic where one exists (passives, tact switch, AO3400A); extended: J1, J2, U1, U2, SW4, D1",
   "why": "Cheapest available; product.md BOM",
   "phase": "P3",
   "ts": "2026-10-28T11:17:23"
  },
  {
   "what": "EasyEDA courtyards grown to pads + 0.25 mm by kicad/gen/fix_courtyards.py; pin types set by kicad/gen/pin_types.py",
   "why": "lib_pull ships body-outline courtyards and all-unspecified pins (filed to hive-hwde)",
   "phase": "P3",
   "ts": "2026-10-28T11:17:23"
  },
  {
   "what": "Schematic review W3: unused TCA9535 pins pulled down together by R19 10k",
   "why": "A floating input toggles INT and the TCA9535 has no interrupt mask; one resistor, not a hard GND tie, so a pin set as output by mistake fights 10k",
   "phase": "P4",
   "ts": "2026-10-28T11:35:38"
  },
  {
   "what": "Schematic review W5: backlight resistors now 3 x 120R 0603 (40R, 39-61 mA, 50 mW each)",
   "why": "2 x 75R ran each 0603 at 80% of rating; no basic 0805/1206 value fits",
   "phase": "P4",
   "ts": "2026-10-28T11:35:38"
  },
  {
   "what": "Schematic review W1/W4/W6/I3 handled in docs and firmware notes: SPI <= 15 MHz, LED off-states, core strapping-pin warning, smooth (detent-free) encoder kept",
   "why": "The LCD's 66 ns write clock; G/B off = output high; the bias lives on core GPIOs; EC11E1834403 is the cheapest EC11 with push and a smooth volume knob is normal in hi-fi (EC11E18244A5 is the detented drop-in)",
   "phase": "P4",
   "ts": "2026-10-28T11:35:39"
  },
